        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-31T23:49:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Technically on existing devices it would be more correct to call getFwmarkForNetwork in the code that configures these map entries (since in theory the internal structure of the fwmark is not an API that mainline code can rely on). That won\u0027t define the protect from VPN bit but it will at least define this value.\n\nWe could add field metrics to detect if anyone has changed it - whenever a network connects, some percentage of the time we could call getFwmarkForNetwork and see if the mask is not exactly 0xffff.\n\nFor new releases, it\u0027s probably time we make it possible to actually rely on this. Perhaps not make it a formal API, but at least test it in CTS so we don\u0027t have to guess/detect/measure.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "b45afd25cf5dadfb1c52711067e1e99185e731f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
