        "id": 1594463
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-31T15:24:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, we have support for protecting your sockets from VPN on a given network. Let\u0027s say you protect your sockets from VPN on network A, do you really want to receive packets from network B?\n\nAs I am writing this, I also notice that fwmark_reflect does not seem to take into account the listening sockets mark. I think a correct implementation should not reflect the incoming packets mark into the packet if the listening socket has set a mark, but should use the mark of the listening socket instead. So I think in this scenario, a listening socket could successfully receive (and acknowledge) tcp packets from a network it is not allowed to access.",
      "parentUuid": "3b49263e_70819c72",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 407,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 407,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "b45afd25cf5dadfb1c52711067e1e99185e731f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1086d97_592d8609",
        "filename": "bpf/progs/netd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 407,
      "author": {
        "id": 1594463
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-31T15:27:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alternatively, I wonder whether we should do this check on all incoming packets: if a network is explicitly selected, drop it if the netids do not match. That way the synack will succeed, but the accepting socket will not be able to receive any packets.",
      "parentUuid": "583f58d5_d77c95ee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 407,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 407,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "b45afd25cf5dadfb1c52711067e1e99185e731f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
